---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="About Us — Independent Bra Sizing Tools & Guides | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Learn about BraSizeChecker, our independent modern bra sizing methodology, team transparency, privacy commitments, and fit limitations."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/about"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About Us' }]} />
    
    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Product Transparency
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        About BraSizeChecker
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        BraSizeChecker is an independent digital tool and reference hub designed to help individuals find an accurate starting bra size from home using modern fitting standards.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <!-- Section 1: Why BraSizeChecker Exists -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Why BraSizeChecker Exists</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          For decades, traditional bra fitting guides relied on the outdated "+4 method"—adding 4 to 5 inches to a person's underbust measurement. This resulted in millions of people wearing band sizes that were far too loose and cup sizes that were far too small.
        </p>
        <p>
          BraSizeChecker was created to provide a modern, direct underbust calculation algorithm that anchors the bra band snugly against the ribcage where 80% of support belongs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Independent & Unbiased -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">100% Independent & Brand-Neutral</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          BraSizeChecker is completely independent. We are not owned, operated, or sponsored by any lingerie manufacturer, brand, or retail outlet.
        </p>
        <p class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl border border-hairline font-medium text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink">
          &bull; Zero paid product placements &bull; Objective conversion algorithms &bull; Unbiased fit advice
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Transparency & Limitations -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Understanding Sizing Limitations</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          While our calculator provides a highly accurate modern fitting baseline, a calculated size is always a <strong>starting point, not a guaranteed medical prescription</strong>.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-body mb-4">
          <li><strong>Fabric Elasticity:</strong> Firm powernet elastic fits tighter than soft microfiber of the same size label.</li>
          <li><strong>Cup Construction:</strong> Molded foam cups hold a fixed shape, whereas seamed fabric cups conform flexibly.</li>
          <li><strong>Body Asymmetry:</strong> Most human bodies have slight breast size variations that require fitting the larger side.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/methodology" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline text-xs sm:text-sm">Read full methodology documentation &rarr;</a>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Privacy & Maintenance -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Privacy & Editorial Team</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Our calculator processes all underbust and bust inputs locally inside your browser. We do not create user profiles, require account sign-ups, or store personal measurement data.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-4">
          All educational guides are researched, written, and maintained by the <strong>BraSizeChecker Editorial & Product Team</strong> with continuous updates.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-xs font-bold">
          <a href="/contact" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-primary text-white rounded-xl hover:bg-primary-hover transition-colors shadow-2xs">Contact Our Team &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/privacy-policy" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-surface border border-hairline text-ink rounded-xl hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 transition-colors">Privacy Policy &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
